    {
      "id": 227,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -2024.522631021042,
        4415.50386067693
      ],
      "size": [
        735.6586525669613,
        405.6171760437146
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 12,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MarkDKBerry.com\n\nThis is for editing single shot images using Minimax H3 model. (it creates 5 images to get 1 result)\n\n*This approach and workflow came from Ryko (ryko2467) on discord.*\n\n## MODELS REQUIRED\n\n- then use FL2VA Minimax Model (I havent tried ref model with this one but it wasnt working for the image creation for some reason). using fl2va model as that what was in it originally. </br>\n\n- I tried once with ref model and it didnt behave so went back to FL2VA int8 model\n\n\n## TESTS:\n\n*it fixes up bad eyes and faces without asking it to which is good, but the general use is a bit hit and miss for my purposes so far. maybe it is how you use it that matters*\n\n- changed the hair on a person just by prompting: `change the hair of the woman on the left to be black with a bob cut` </br>\n\n- this didnt work it just straight used the entire picture 2: `replace the man in the middle of <Picture 1> with the man from <Picture 2>` </br>\n\n- this replaced the man in the middle, and put a white area around him and he wasnt blended in at all it was straight crop and paste from picture 2: `replace the man on the right of <Picture 1> with the man from <Picture 2>. dont change anything else in <picture 1>`"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# MarkDKBerry.com\n\nThis is for editing single shot images using Minimax H3 model. (it creates 5 images to get 1 result)\n\n*This approach and workflow came from Ryko (ryko2467) on discord.*\n\n## MODELS REQUIRED\n\n- then use FL2VA Minimax Model (I havent tried ref model with this one but it wasnt working for the image creation for some reason). using fl2va model as that what was in it originally. </br>\n\n- I tried once with ref model and it didnt behave so went back to FL2VA int8 model\n\n\n## TESTS:\n\n*it fixes up bad eyes and faces without asking it to which is good, but the general use is a bit hit and miss for my purposes so far. maybe it is how you use it that matters*\n\n- changed the hair on a person just by prompting: `change the hair of the woman on the left to be black with a bob cut` </br>\n\n- this didnt work it just straight used the entire picture 2: `replace the man in the middle of <Picture 1> with the man from <Picture 2>` </br>\n\n- this replaced the man in the middle, and put a white area around him and he wasnt blended in at all it was straight crop and paste from picture 2: `replace the man on the right of <Picture 1> with the man from <Picture 2>. dont change anything else in <picture 1>`"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
